@title Electronic health record downtime runbook
@subtitle For charge nurses and front-desk staff. Effective 2026-11-15
@author Pelican Bay Clinic, Clinical Operations

## Declare downtime
Downtime is declared when the record has been unavailable or unusably slow for 10 minutes.
- The charge nurse announces "Paper procedures" on the overhead page.
- The charge nurse calls the IT service desk on extension 5000.

## During downtime
1. Switch to paper.
-- a) Take the downtime binder from each station. It holds the printed schedule, refreshed at 05:00 daily, plus an allergy list and a medication list for every patient booked that day.
-- b) Label every paper form with a patient label sheet.
2. Check in patients.
-- a) Confirm identity with two identifiers: name and date of birth.
-- b) Record the arrival time by hand.
3. Orders and medications.
-- a) Write down every verbal order and read it back.
-- b) Never give a high-risk medication without a second nurse's check.
-- c) Record every dose on the paper medication sheet.
4. Keep care moving.
-- a) Do not cancel visits solely because of downtime.
-- b) Tell patients about any delay beyond 20 minutes.

!! The allergy list in the binder is the source of truth until the record is back.

## Recovery
- a) When IT announces restoration, wait for the all-clear before entering anything.
- b) Scan paper documents into the record within 4 hours.
- c) Reconcile medication entries within 24 hours.
- d) Report the event on the incident form.

!!! If any paper forms are lost, tell the privacy officer at once.

